---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const engines = [
  {
    format: 'GGUF',
    pkg: 'llama.cpp-mac-arm64-apple-metal-advsimd',
    version: '2.29.1',
    note: 'Metal llama.cpp engine — serves every GGUF-format run.',
  },
  {
    format: 'MLX',
    pkg: 'mlx-llm-mac-arm64-apple-metal-nax-advsimd',
    version: '1.11.0',
    note: 'NA-aware MLX engine (note the nax segment) — serves every MLX-format run.',
  },
];
const capturedAt = '2026-08-25';

const changelog = [
  {
    date: '2026-08-22',
    text: 'Began tracking; confirmed NA-aware MLX engine (1.11.0 nax) active for all MLX runs; llama.cpp Metal 2.29.1 for GGUF.',
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Runtime Version Tracking"
  description="A silent inference-engine update between rounds is an invisible confound. Our policy: auto-update off, engine versions captured per run, deliberate review before any bump."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Lab · Transparency</p>
    <h1>Runtime Version Tracking</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every score on this site was produced by an inference engine with an exact version.
      This page says which ones, and commits us to never letting that change silently.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="lab-status">Transparency commitment &middot; started 2026-08-22 &middot; engine table and changelog updated with every change</p>

  <section class="lab-section">
    <h2>Why engine versions matter</h2>
    <p>
      A local-model benchmark has two version numbers that matter: the model&rsquo;s and the
      inference engine&rsquo;s. The second one is the one almost nobody tracks. Engines ship
      real performance and behavior changes &mdash; new kernels, new hardware support, sampler
      fixes &mdash; and runners like LM Studio can auto-update the selected engine in the
      background, with no prompt and no visible notice.
    </p>
    <p>
      That means a <strong>silent engine update between rounds is an invisible confound on
      every round-over-round comparison</strong>: a model can appear faster or slower, or even
      score differently, when nothing about the model changed at all. This is a real gap we
      found in our own setup &mdash; auto-update was on, a pending MLX engine bump
      (1.10.1&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;1.11.0) was sitting unannounced in the runtimes panel, and no
      run manifest we had ever produced recorded which engine build served it. We closed the
      gap, and this page is the public side of that fix.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="lab-section">
    <h2>The policy</h2>
    <ul class="policy-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Runtime auto-update is OFF on the bench host.</strong> Engine versions do not
        change underneath a test series.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Engine versions are captured per run.</strong> The runtime listing (exact
        package name and version, per model format) is recorded into the benchmark manifest,
        so every archived result names the engine that produced it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Engine updates get a deliberate review before adoption.</strong> When an update
        is pending, we read the release notes, assess what it could affect in prior results,
        adopt it at a round boundary &mdash; and log it in the changelog below.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="lab-section">
    <h2>Current engines <span class="sec-date">captured live {capturedAt}</span></h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="lab-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Model format</th><th>Selected engine</th><th>Version</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {engines.map((e) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{e.format}</td>
              <td><code>{e.pkg}</code></td>
              <td class="num">{e.version}</td>
              <td>{e.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="table-note">
      Older engine versions remain installed but unselected (llama.cpp back to 2.24.0, MLX
      back to 1.8.5, in both generic and <code>nax</code> variants) &mdash; useful if a
      regression ever needs to be bisected against a prior engine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="lab-section">
    <h2>Engine changelog</h2>
    <p>
      One entry per engine event &mdash; tracking milestones and every adopted update. Future
      engine bumps will appear here with what changed and what it might mean for comparisons
      across the boundary.
    </p>
    <ul class="changelog">
      {changelog.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <span class="cl-date">{c.date}</span>
          <span class="cl-text">{c.text}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
      <li class="pending">
        <span class="cl-date">next</span>
        <span class="cl-text">The next engine update will be reviewed and logged here before it serves a single scored run.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="lab-back"><a href="/lab/">&larr; Back to the Lab</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lab-status {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 18px 0 0;
  }
  .lab-status::before { content: '\25B8 '; color: var(--green); }

  .lab-section { margin: 40px 0 0; max-width: 820px; }
  .lab-section h2 {
    font-size: 21px;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    padding-top: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
  }
  .sec-date {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-left: 10px;
    vertical-align: 2px;
  }
  .lab-section p, .lab-section li { color: var(--text-dim); }
  .lab-section code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.86em;
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .policy-list { padding-left: 22px; }
  .policy-list li { margin: 0 0 12px; }

  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 18px 0 10px; }
  .lab-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 14px;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .lab-table th {
    text-align: left;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .lab-table td {
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    color: var(--text-dim);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .lab-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .lab-table td.num { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--green); white-space: nowrap; }
  .table-note { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }

  .changelog { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 16px 0 0; }
  .changelog li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
  }
  .changelog li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .cl-date {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--green);
    white-space: nowrap;
    min-width: 88px;
  }
  .changelog li.pending .cl-date { color: var(--muted); }
  .changelog li.pending .cl-text { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }
  .cl-text { font-size: 14px; }

  .lab-back { margin: 40px 0 40px; }
</style>
